  canonical_controls: { category: "E", userRefColumns: ["published_by_user_id"], piiRisk: "none", rlsStatus: "none", specialHandling: "GLOBAL SecureLogic canonical control identity (VA-S4 Step 1, 20261067) — a reusable assurance CONCEPT, never a framework requirement and never tenant data. No organization_id, no RLS: there is structurally nothing here to leak. Same shape as canonical_products, deliberately a different table (a control is not a product). Published content is FROZEN by canonical_controls_publication_guard — a correction is a NEW superseding row, never an in-place edit, so a past assurance decision stays reconstructible. published_by_user_id is a GOVERNANCE ACTOR, not PII, and its FK is ON DELETE RESTRICT on purpose: a published decision must keep naming the human who published it (the publication-authority CHECK would reject a NULL anyway). LEAVE on user delete; RESTRICT never fires under tombstone O-3. Written only through the elevated publication path (scripts/publish-canonical-controls.ts); app_request has SELECT only." },
